# AI Agent Instructions & Rules

You are an AI assistant working on the **YoutubeCreatorAssistant** project (a.k.a. CreatorHub).
Please read and strictly follow these rules during all sessions.

## 1. Command Bundling Rule (CRITICAL)
- **Rule:** All sequential terminal commands proposed by the AI assistant MUST be bundled together into a single executable command line to reduce repetitive approval prompts.
- **PowerShell (Default OS is Windows):** Separate commands using a semicolon `;`. Do NOT use `&&` (which is not supported in older PowerShell or can fail depending on settings).
  * Example: `git add .; git commit -m "commit message"; git push`
- **Linux/Bash/CMD:** Separate commands using double ampersands `&&` or semicolons `;`.
- **Reference:** For details and examples, refer to [docs/BUNDLED_COMMANDS_RULE.md](file:///e:/KHOA/HAPPY_CODING/CODER%20THAN%20THANH/YoutubeCreatorAssistant/docs/BUNDLED_COMMANDS_RULE.md).

## 2. Technology Stack & Coding Standards
- **Frontend:** Angular 21+ using Signals, Standalone Components, and the modern `@defer` block.
  - Follow the standards in [docs/CLEAN_CODE.md](file:///e:/KHOA/HAPPY_CODING/CODER%20THAN%20THANH/YoutubeCreatorAssistant/docs/CLEAN_CODE.md).
  - Use RxJS only where necessary, preferring Signal-based state and reactive routing parameter derivation to avoid HTTP race conditions.
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express, TypeScript, and Prisma ORM with SQLite database.
  - Ensure relational integrity (e.g., Episode-Asset many-to-many relationship).
  - Follow clean MVC-like controller/endpoint structures in `server.ts`.

## 3. Tool Usage Best Practices
- **Editing Files:** Use precise replacement tools (`replace_file_content` or `multi_replace_file_content`) instead of full-file rewrites to minimize token cost and avoid errors.
- **Running Tests:** Always run unit tests (`npm test` in backend and frontend) and E2E tests (`cypress` or equivalent) after modifying code to verify functionality.
- **No Placeholders:** Never use placeholders in source code. All functions, components, and templates must be fully implemented.
